    "body": "## Description\n\nQuote each `SchedulingSpec.env_vars` assignment with `shlex.quote()` when generating Slurm Apptainer commands. This keeps the complete `KEY=VALUE` in one `--env` argument when the batch script is parsed by the outer shell.\n\n### Affected scenarios\n\n- JSON configuration containing spaces, quotes, and commas.\n- Paths containing spaces, such as `/models/model cache`.\n- Text containing single/double quotes, newlines, or literal shell metacharacters.\n- Empty values.\n\nPreviously, these values could be split into multiple arguments or lose quote characters. Real Apptainer tests reproduce whitespace/JSON values being misinterpreted as the image path, failing before container execution. Ordinary numeric/plain-text values retain their behavior.\n\n### Compatibility boundary\n\n- Only Slurm's `container_type=\"apptainer\"` command-generation path changes.\n- No HTTP/OSS implementation, configuration fields, or dependencies are included.\n- Native Slurm, Ray, and LocalScheduler are unchanged.\n- Callers should provide raw, resolved values rather than prequoted shell fragments. Configurations relying on implicit outer-shell variable expansion, command substitution, globbing, or tilde expansion should resolve those expressions before constructing `env_vars`.\n- Apptainer's own environment evaluation is unchanged. This does not add `--no-eval` or guarantee literal preservation of arbitrary expressions inside the container.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nNo linked issue; independently reproduced with generated shell commands and a real Apptainer container.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix\n- [ ] ✨ New feature\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [ ] ✅ Test coverage improvement\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/areal-project/community/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`)\n- [x] Relevant tests pass; new tests added for new functionality\n- [ ] Documentation updated (if applicable; built with `./docs/build_all.sh`)\n- [x] Branch is up to date with `main`\n- [ ] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command\n- [x] This PR was created by a coding agent via `/create-pr`\n- [ ] This PR is a breaking change\n\n**Breaking Change Details (if applicable):** No schema or API changes. See the outer-shell expansion compatibility note above.\n\n## Additional Context\n\n- `pytest tests/test_slurm_reservation_and_env.py -q`: **58 passed** in a CPU-only container after rebasing onto the latest main.\n- Changed-file pre-commit hooks pass. The full-repository run was attempted but is not fully green: lockfile regeneration encountered an existing upstream wheel's TLS certificate error; the CLI generator also reported changes during concurrent staging, with no generated-document diff retained. No dependency, lockfile, or documentation changes are included.\n- Apptainer **1.3.2** smoke: quoted numeric, whitespace-path, JSON, mixed-quote, newline, and empty values arrive unchanged. A separate `$(...)` probe confirms runtime-side evaluation still occurs.\n- Unit tests capture real Bash-parsed arguments using a mocked `srun`; CI does not require Slurm or Apptainer for these regression cases.\n",
